  "notes": "{看過|かんか} means to overlook or ignore something, often used critically to indicate negligence.\n\nWRITING:\n- {看|かん} (watch, look)\n- {過|か} (pass by, exceed)\n\nUSAGE:\n- {看過|かんか}する (to overlook - suru verb)\n- {看過|かんか}できない (cannot overlook)\n- {看過|かんか}し{得|え}ない (cannot be allowed to pass)\n- Often used in negative contexts\n- Implies criticism of inaction\n- Formal/written style\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜を{看過|かんか}できない (cannot overlook ~)\n- {看過|かんか}するわけにはいかない (cannot let it pass)\n- {看過|かんか}し{難|がた}い{問題|もんだい} (a problem difficult to ignore)\n\nREGISTER:\n- Literary/formal expression\n- Common in news, official statements\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {見過|みす}ごす (to overlook - less formal)\n- {黙認|もくにん} (tacit approval)\n- {無視|むし}する (to ignore)",
